Package: ecologytools
Title: Utilities and Data Visualization Tools for Ecology
Version: 1.1
Authors@R:
    person("Ryan", "Martin", email = "ryanmartin@uidaho.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Provides custom functions, plotting utilities, and quantitative
    tools for ecological data analysis and visualization. Plotting tools
    include the theme_martin() ggplot2 theme and the Martin colour palettes
    (pal(), scale_color_martin(), scale_fill_martin()) for publication-style
    figures. Spatial and terrain utilities built on 'terra' provide raster
    aggregation, days since peak instantaneous rate of green-up, distance to
    escape terrain, vector ruggedness measures, raster summaries, and
    in-memory packing of rasters, together with DBSCAN-based clustering of GPS
    locations into search areas. Forage and diet tools include modal phenology
    summaries, plant forage-quality and diet-proportion summaries, and the
    fresh() function for evaluating habitat-scale forage resources for
    generalist herbivores via linear programming.
